text.paragraph:
Corneal edema has been reported in patients taking amantadine. Symptoms include sudden onset of blurry vision, or progressive vision loss, with or without eye pain. Corneal involvement is usually bilateral. Onset can occur from a few weeks to several years after starting amantadine. Resolution of symptoms typically begins within weeks of amantadine cessation. However, corneal grafts have been required in some patients when the condition is not recognized. Permanent damage can occur if amantadine is continued. Ask patients if their vision has changed and obtain ophthalmologic examinations to rule out corneal edema should vision changes occur after initiation of therapy with Amantadine Hydrochloride Oral Solution USP 50 mg/5 mL. If corneal edema occurs, taper and discontinue Amantadine Hydrochloride Oral Solution USP 50 mg/5 mL [
                              see Dosage and Administration
                           ].
